+## Password-change form
+
+Keep the existing account-category `비밀번호 변경` entry and inline form. Do not open another ordinary modal or add an account selector. Only the current user can change their password; even a superuser gets no target-user field or proxy operation. Preserve the real server self-only/current-password checks.
+
+The existing change contract contains **현재 비밀번호** and **새 비밀번호**, so keep exactly those fields. Do not import installation's separate password-confirmation stage into this form or invent a confirmation field without an explicit change-form contract. No email/profile editor, reveal toggle, password reset, strength meter, minimum-length/complexity/pattern policy or L2/L3 gate is added. Password policy remains unresolved; presentation must not settle it.
+
+At the top of the form, before the first field and submit, show the existing impact notice in warning surface/status-warning with visible text: `바꾸면 이 계정의 모든 세션과 모든 액세스 토큰이 끊깁니다. 다시 로그인해야 하고, 발급해 둔 액세스 토큰도 다시 발급해야 합니다.` This applies only to password change; never place the same warning on logout. Do not expose counts, token names or secret values. The notice describes existing server effects, not a new confirmation stage.
+
+Form width ≤560px within the existing panel; shared native Field/Input controls, 36px minimum height, label 13/20px, input 14/22px, 20px field gap and 24px before the submit action. Keep masked `type=password`, stable names `current`/`next`, respective `autocomplete=current-password`/`new-password`, visible labels and unchanged native values. Paste/autofill/password managers must work; do not trim, normalize or log credentials. Warning and all controls remain reachable at #61's narrow effective width.
+
+One explicit submit action, `바꾸기` (accessible name may clarify `비밀번호 바꾸기`), invokes the existing callback with exact `{current,next}` values. No on-change/blur request. A synchronous reentry guard plus Promise-backed disabled/pending state prevents same-tick/keyboard duplicate submission. While pending show `변경 중…` and `aria-busy`; maintain input values and native focus. IME composition-ending Enter is not submission. Catch actual synchronous/asynchronous rejection and release the guard; a missing callback is an unavailable operation, not success.
+
+| Outcome | Required scoped presentation |
+| --- | --- |
+| `wrong-password` | Existing `현재 비밀번호가 올바르지 않습니다`, connected to current field with aria-invalid |
+| `empty-password` | Existing `새 비밀번호를 입력하세요`, connected to new field with aria-invalid |
+| `self-only` / `unknown-account` | Existing safe mapped form-level messages; do not blame a password field or reveal another account |
+| Unknown returned rule / thrown request failure | `비밀번호를 바꾸지 못했습니다. 잠시 후 다시 시도하십시오.`; no raw unknown code, exception or stack |
+| Callback success | Existing parent clears invalidated session/cache and returns to login; do not display a local success toast immediately before unmount or fabricate authenticated state |
+
+Start with no red error. Mark only a deterministically identified field invalid, retain masked values for correction and clear stale field feedback when edited without running authentication. A failed change does not invalidate any PAT or session; verify actual backend behavior rather than implying it through copy. A successful change invalidates every live PAT and every session of this account including current, while other accounts stay unaffected; existing audit behavior must not change. Explicit submission is the operation, not merely a client-side field-validation success.
+
+When a parent/session-refresh failure obscures the successful credential change, this form must not retry automatically or claim the old password still works. The callback currently returns no phase distinction; such a handoff defect must be separately scoped in App/API rather than diagnosed from the component's render. Real login/PAT/session checks supply completion evidence.
+
+## Logout separation and focus
+
+Logout remains the separate existing account-category action outside PasswordChangeForm. It does not submit or validate password fields, change a password, revoke all PATs or claim to terminate all devices. Its contract ends this browser's session without affecting other users. Do not add a sign-out-everywhere option, extra confirmation, new retry path or fake success. #62 may style the existing form boundary so the action is visually distinct; moving/rewiring the AppShell-owned action requires separate scope, not adding a duplicate button inside the form.
+
+Keep #61 category navigation/focus rules and #47 focus ring (2px plus 2px separation). Opening the existing password form may focus current-password once; do not autofocus repeatedly on theme/error renders. Deterministic field failure focuses its field after submission; generic errors are announced without repeatedly stealing focus. Settings changes leave focus on their native select. Password success/logout use the existing login-entry focus path; a missing parent focus handoff is a reported integration gap. No new global keyboard handler or focus trap inside the right panel.
