+## Independent review disposition
+
+Medium 1 accepted (2026-09-17): the original decision required generic request failures without noticing that `App.changeOwnPassword` mapped missing rules to `unknown-account` before the form received them. The decision now explicitly authorizes the minimal existing-callback error adapter correction and requires real adapter-to-form regression evidence. Only recognized HTTP-400 password rules receive rule-specific messages; all other failures retain the existing rejected-Promise path for generic display. No API, authentication policy, successful-session handling or unrelated state wiring is changed by this scope decision. No implementation was performed.
+
+User override accepted: #62 browser verification is now restricted to fresh Playwright-owned isolated Chromium, with no existing/default browser attachment, connectOverCDP to an existing browser, OS/native input injection or broad process kills. Replaced native-IME/real-password-manager mandatory checklist items with scoped DOM-value/autofill and synthetic/CDP event-order evidence plus explicit unverified limitations. Genuine extension-based200% and actual API/persistence/password/session/PAT gates remain required. This changes verification method only; the separately amended per-key preference scope below applies, while default-mode consumption, parent-auth handoff and broader evidence limits remain separate. No implementation or tests were performed.
+
